    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f8bee1d8",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f8bee1d8"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 18. Testing Results &nbsp;<sub>(report &sect;4.3.3)</sub>\n",
        "\n",
        "Greedy evaluation ($\\epsilon = 0$) of the **episode-2400** checkpoint over 100\n",
        "episodes:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Metric | Result |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| Evaluation episodes | 100 |\n",
        "| Episodes completing &ge; 1 lap (completion rate) | 100 (100.00 %) |\n",
        "| Mean laps completed per episode | 1.00 |\n",
        "| Failures: snail / fall / timeout (0 laps) | 0 / 0 / 0 |\n",
        "| Episodes reaching the 600-step cap | 100 |\n",
        "| Average return / average steps | 164.88 / 600.00 |\n",
        "\n",
        "*Table 4.6 &mdash; greedy evaluation of the checkpoint saved at episode 2400.*\n",
        "The agent consistently completes **one** full lap, then moves to a safe zone\n",
        "until the 600-step cap. Every episode runs the full budget, but none registers as\n",
        "a *timeout failure* (reaching the cap with **zero** laps). A second 100-episode\n",
        "run reproduced the result exactly. Three environment bugs were corrected prior to\n",
        "evaluation, all at the environment level (the Q-table was neither retrained nor\n",
        "altered): entity movement not gated to an in-progress step's physics-frame\n",
        "window; a collision-shape write silently rejected by Godot during a physics\n",
        "callback; and a snail-collision signal capable of arriving one episode late."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 19,
      "id": "20674c87",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-29T15:53:08.483200Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-29T15:53:08.482944Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-29T15:53:08.490405Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-29T15:53:08.489781Z"
        },
        "id": "20674c87",
